[b]Flag the countries you care about, just like EU IV, and only get interrupted for them. Plus how many people each event choice affects, and the alerts vanilla is missing.[/b]

Example: a revolution starts in a country on the other side of the world, and vanilla stops you with a toast. During a diplomatic play, you hear about every country picking a side. And an event says "+10.0% of Czech Pops become more Radical": is that 2,000 people or 2 million ?

With Smart Notifications, that revolution goes to your feed, you only hear about the countries on your watchlist, and the event reads "+10.0% of Czech Pops (3.83M nationwide) become more Radical".

[h1]Country watchlist[/h1]
[list]
[*]Flag any country in the world. It starts with the great powers, your neighbors and your rivals.
[*]Diplomatic plays, wars, revolutions and countries joining a side only pop up when you or a watched country is involved. Everything else goes to the feed.
[/list]

[h1]Population in events[/h1]
[list]
[*]Every event, journal entry and decision that moves pops says how many people: cultures, religions, interest groups, professions and strata.
[*]Choices about a state show its size: "in Bohemia (2.1M inhabitants)".
[*]The number is nationwide. For an effect on a single state it is an upper bound, because the game does not give mods the size of a group inside a state.
[*]English game language only for now.
[/list]

[h1]Alerts vanilla is missing[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Mobilized army without general[/b]: the army won't move and its front stalls, and vanilla never tells you.
[*][b]Law ready to enact[/b]: flag the law you're working toward from its panel. You get an alert and one toast the moment it has better odds of passing than stalling.
[*][b]Taxation deficit[/b]: names the state that is short on tax capacity.
[*][b]Truce expired[/b]: a toast when your truce with a country ends.
[*][b]Agitator invite available[/b]: you have a free agitator slot and an exiled character who can fill it.
[/list]

Low-value vanilla toasts and popups also go to the feed or get muted, like an interest group joining a lobby (nearly always something you just did). Losing an actual subject still tells you.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Already played Victoria 3 ?[/h1]

Open Message Settings (the bell icon) and press [b]Reset to Default Settings[/b] once. The game keeps every notification setting you ever changed by hand, and those override any mod. Fresh install: nothing to do.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Game version 1.15.[/b]
[*][b]Achievement compatible.[/b]
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] Add or remove it mid-campaign.
[*][b]Single-player only.[/b]
[*][b]All 11 game languages[/b] (population numbers: English only for now).
[*][b]Conflicts:[/b] it replaces 3 vanilla files: the notification list ([i]common/messages/00_messages.txt[/i]), the Message Settings screen and the law panel. Another notification mod, or a UI mod that reworks those screens, will clash. Whichever loads last wins.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]My other mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3814823352][b][u]Smart Treaties[/u][/b][/url]: see what each goods transfer earns or costs you before you sign, and the 5 most profitable deals you could propose.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3803950977][b][u]Build All[/u][/b][/url]: one click to queue a building in every state that can take it. Life changing for electrification.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Reporting Issues[/h1]

If something's off, include:
[list]
[*] What you expected vs. what happened.
[*] Your Victoria 3 version and other mods enabled.
[*] Whether you had pressed "Reset to Default Settings" before playing
[*] A screenshot if it is something you can see.
[/list]

Source and issue tracker: [url=https://github.com/dcoullon/victoria3-smart-notifications]https://github.com/dcoullon/victoria3-smart-notifications[/url]

If the mod helps you, a thumbs up below the screenshots lets other players find it too !
